    "title": "Account Management & Data Governance",
    "body": "### 2.1 RBAC — the #1 source of tricky questions\n\nPrivileges are granted to roles, never directly to users. Users are granted roles; roles can be granted to other roles (inheritance). Secondary roles let a session activate multiple roles at once.\n\n| System role | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORGADMIN | Organization-level operations across accounts |\n| ACCOUNTADMIN | Full account authority — use sparingly |\n| SECURITYADMIN | Manages users, roles, and grants globally |\n| USERADMIN | Creates users and roles (child of SECURITYADMIN) |\n| SYSADMIN | Recommended parent for creating DBs, schemas, warehouses |\n| PUBLIC | Default role every user holds |\n\n> **Trap: ACCOUNTADMIN does NOT automatically see custom roles. Best practice is a custom role hierarchy rolled up under SYSADMIN.**\n\n### 2.1 Authentication & network\n\nMFA (recommended for all), SSO via SAML 2.0, OAuth (Snowflake as provider or client), key-pair auth (service accounts, Snowpipe). Network policies allow/block IPs at account or user level; private connectivity via AWS PrivateLink, Azure Private Link, Google Private Service Connect. Tri-Secret Secure (Business Critical+) combines customer-managed keys with Snowflake keys. Trust CenterNew · C03 is the security-posture dashboard: MFA coverage, network policy usage, risky configurations.\n\n### 2.2 Data governance\n\n```sql\n-- Dynamic data masking by role\r\nCREATE OR REPLACE MASKING POLICY ssn_mask AS (val STRING) RETURNS STRING ->\r\n  CASE WHEN CURRENT_ROLE() IN ('HR_ADMIN') THEN val\r\n       ELSE REGEXP_REPLACE(val, '.', '*', 1, 5) END;\r\nALTER TABLE employees MODIFY COLUMN ssn SET MASKING POLICY ssn_mask;\n```\n\nKnow all of: dynamic data masking, row access policies, secure views/UDFs, object tagging, automatic classification, data lineageNew · C03 , and Data Clean RoomsNew · C03 (privacy-preserving joint analytics).\n\n### 2.3 Monitoring & cost\n\nResource Monitors set credit quotas with actions: notify, suspend (finish running queries), suspend immediate (kill them). ACCOUNT_USAGE and ORGANIZATION_USAGE schemas expose credit and storage history. Warehouse credit math: each size doubles credits/hour (XS = 1, S = 2, M = 4, L = 8, XL = 16...); billed per second with a 60-second minimum on resume.\n\n### Topic checklist",
