    "title": "Data Loading, Unloading & Connectivity",
    "body": "### 3.1 Stages — know the symbols cold\n\n| Stage | Syntax | Use case |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| User stage | @~ | Personal staging, one per user |\n| Table stage | @%tablename | Files destined for one table |\n| Named internal | @stage_name | Shared team staging inside Snowflake |\n| Named external | @stage_name | Points at S3 / Azure Blob / GCS via a storage integration |\n\n### 3.1 COPY INTO — bulk loading\n\n```sql\nCOPY INTO my_table\r\nFROM @my_stage/data/\r\nFILE_FORMAT = (TYPE = PARQUET)\r\nON_ERROR = 'CONTINUE'\r\nPURGE = TRUE;\n```\n\nError handling options: CONTINUE, SKIP_FILE, SKIP_FILE_n%, ABORT_STATEMENT. Transformations during load: column reorder, casts, $1:field for semi-structured. File formats: CSV, JSON, Parquet, Avro, ORC, XML. Unloading is COPY INTO @stage — direction reverses.\n\n### 3.2 Snowpipe vs Snowpipe Streaming\n\n| Feature | Snowpipe | Snowpipe Streaming New · C03 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Latency | Minutes (micro-batch) | Seconds (row-level) |\n| Trigger | Cloud event notifications or REST API | Snowflake Ingest SDK |\n| Compute | Serverless (Snowflake-managed) | Serverless |\n| Use case | Files landing in a stage | CDC, clickstream, IoT |\n\n> **Trap: Different SDKs, different latency, different pricing. If the scenario says files in a stage, it is Snowpipe. If it says rows arriving continuously with seconds-level freshness, it is Snowpipe Streaming.**\n\n### 3.2 Streams, Tasks & Dynamic Tables\n\n```sql\n-- Dynamic Table: declarative pipeline (C03)\r\nCREATE OR REPLACE DYNAMIC TABLE orders_enriched\r\n  TARGET_LAG = '1 minute'\r\n  WAREHOUSE = xfm_wh\r\nAS SELECT o.*, c.segment\r\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c USING (customer_id);\n```\n\nDecision rule: target-state thinking + automatic refresh → Dynamic Table. CDC semantics + custom MERGE logic → Streams + Tasks. Append-only processing → append-only streams. Openflow appears in the blueprint but the official guide excludes it from scored questions until globally GA; verify the current study guide PDF before your date.\n\n### 3.3 Connectors & integrations\n\nKafka Connector, Spark Connector, drivers (JDBC/ODBC/Python/Go/.NET/Node.js). Storage integrations grant IAM-based access to external stages without embedding credentials. API integrations back external functions. Git integration counts here too.\n\n### Topic checklist",
