    "body": "### 5.1 Time Travel & Fail-safe\n\nTime Travel: user-accessible via AT | BEFORE and UNDROP; 1 day default, up to 90 days on Enterprise+ for permanent tables. Fail-safe: 7 additional days after Time Travel, recoverable only by Snowflake support.\n\n> **Trap: Transient and temporary tables get short Time Travel but NO Fail-safe. The exam loves this distinction — and it is why transient tables cost less to store.**\n\n### 5.3 Cloning & replication\n\nZero-copy cloning of tables, schemas, and databases is a metadata operation — no storage cost until data diverges. Replication copies databases or accounts across regions and clouds; failover groups (Business Critical+) orchestrate controlled failover.\n\n### 5.2 Sharing mechanisms — pick the right one\n\n| Mechanism | Cross-region / cloud? | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Direct share | No — same region only | Zero-copy; consumer imports the share |\n| Reader account | No | Provider-managed account for consumers without Snowflake |\n| Marketplace listing | Yes | Public or private data products |\n| Replication | Yes | Required before sharing across regions directly |\n| Native Apps New · C03 | Yes | Packaged applications distributed via Marketplace |\n| Data Clean Rooms New · C03 | Yes | Joint analytics without exposing raw PII |\n\n> **Trap: if the scenario says cross-region, \"direct share\" is wrong. Replicate first, or use a listing.**\n\n### Topic checklist",
